          text: 'Each carbon is written with the hydrogens attached to it, left to right along the chain: $\\ce{CH3COCH2CH3}$. Parentheses mark a branch on the preceding carbon, $\\ce{CH3CH(CH3)CH3}$, or repeated units, $\\ce{CH3(CH2)4CH3}$. A $\\ce{CO}$ inside a chain means $\\ce{C=O}$, and $\\ce{CHO}$ at the end means an aldehyde, $\\ce{-CH=O}$.',
